FILE: vUX-formValidator.js
FEATURE: component-teardown
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'resizer-docs'

REASON
Two changes.

The three document listeners bound by addEventhandler() ('transitionend', 'focusin',
'click') were anonymous, so a validator whose form was swapped out by the SPA engine kept
clearing messages and reacting to feedback buttons on a form that no longer existed. They
are now named, with a mirrored removeEventhandler(), and destroy() detaches them and
removes the overlay injected into the form. The 'config.modal' displayer is deliberately
left alone: it is supplied by the consumer and may be in use elsewhere.

Separately, createLoader() called $$.sm(loader).center() while the loader was still
detached. center() reads parentNode.scrollHeight on its static-element branch, and a
detached element computes 'position: static', so this threw
'Cannot read properties of null' on initialize() under the default configuration
(progressAnimationType 'default', loaderLocation 'form'). The loader is now inserted
before it is centred, and given an inline 'position: absolute' so that center() takes its
transform branch deterministically rather than depending on whether the asynchronously
linked formValidator.css has arrived yet.

